It has been reported that the peak positions of the G band of graphene with armchair edges are higher than those with zigzag edges [ 72 ]. The peak position of the G band shifts closer to the D’ band in the case of graphene with armchair edges. This is mainly because of the presence of DUO on graphene with armchair edges since the bond length of C=C on DUO is shorter than others, leading to a stronger force constant and a higher wavenumber shift using the following well-known equation (Eq.  1 ) [ 79 ,  80 ,  83 ,  95 ]. The DUO on graphene calculated in this work also showed the D’ band (Fig.  4 i) due to the short bond length of C=C of DUO (0.1355 nm) (Fig.  7 i), leading to a higher force constant than other C=C bonds in the basal plane of graphene (0.140–0.143 nm) (Fig.  7 i). According to the following equation, the peak position,  ν , can be calculated from the force constant,  k , (Eq.  1 ), 1 ν = k / μ / 2 π c \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
